We eat the small fruit cake.
It tastes really wonderful.
The evening is slowly coming to an end.
I thank her for the great food and the good time.
"The evening has gone by so quickly," I say.
"I am glad that you came," Nele answers.
I take my backpack and put it on.
We go to the door together.
Nele smiles at me.
"Next time I will visit you," she promises.
"That is a great idea!" I answer.
"I will show you my flat then."
"I will definitely come," Nele says.
We say goodbye warmly.
I am very happy.
I think that we are real friends now.
I walk to the U-Bahn.
The mild spring air on the way is wonderful.
